  "notes": [
    "All USD amounts in millions except EPS; shares in millions. Ratios are fractions. Null means not separately available, not zero.",
    "FY2023, FY2024, FY2025 and FY2026 are 52-week fiscal years; all shown quarters 13 weeks, 9M periods 39 weeks. FY2026 ends December 26, 2026.",
    "Q4 flow values are FY2025 minus 9M2025. Q4 weighted shares use 4*FY minus 3*9M, subject to reported rounding. Q4 EPS is net income divided by derived shares, not a separately reported quarterly EPS.",
    "TTM equals last fiscal year less comparable prior nine months plus current nine months. TTM weighted shares are time-weighted combinations; TTM EPS is computed on those shares, not a reported annual EPS.",
    "Q2/Q3 standalone cash-flow figures are differences of cumulative filings. SBC expense is directly reported or Q4 annual-minus-9M, not divided from annual expense.",
    "SBC CF addback, income-statement expense, and equity credit are distinct fields. Capitalized SBC is not separately quantified in the inspected disclosures; no invented capitalized SBC or inferred expense from equity credit.",
    "da_cf is the cash-flow statement line titled depreciation and amortization despite its us-gaap:Depreciation tag. It includes broader D&A; acquired intangible amortization is disclosed separately in the intangible-assets note. Software amortization is not separately quantified. Do not add acquired amortization to da_cf a second time.",
    "Segment gross profit and net contribution are management segment measures and exclude corporate allocations. Segment margins are not consolidated GAAP margins; net contribution is not segment operating income.",
    "CFO less gross PP&E purchases is an unadjusted cash proxy. It does not subtract acquisitions or equity investments, does not net asset-sale proceeds, and does not add SBC back a second time.",
    "Trade working capital = net accounts receivable + net inventories - accounts payable; it is not total operating working capital or the cash-flow working-capital movement.",
    "Restructuring, factory startup, gains on divestitures, equity-method income, acquisition spending, and tax effects remain separate factual lines. None is automatically added back to earnings.",
    "Q3 2026 GAAP SBC expense of 8.835m differs from issuer non-GAAP reconciliation SBC of 8.802m. 9M GAAP SBC 25.556m differs from issuer reconciliation 25.395m; the 0.161m difference equals Note 7 restructuring SBC and must not be double counted. The 0.033m quarterly difference is not independently assigned here.",
    "Factory startup remains in historical expense, including Q3 2026 6.375m; this dataset does not remove factory startup or underutilization costs.",
    "The October 6, 2026 Teradyne $300m equity investment agreement is subsequent to Q3 and pending as of November 3 filing; historical cash/share balances exclude any assumed closing.",
    "Small changes in totals may reflect rounding at the source. Equity-method income when absent as separate tag is reconciled as net income minus pretax income plus tax expense.",
    "Prior TTM capex 100.008m includes the June 2025 Farmers Branch purchase of 55.0m disclosed in Q3 FY2025 MD&A. Current TTM capex 75.752m excludes that purchase by period timing; do not extrapolate a permanently lower capex rate."
  ],
